### GPL component note

ffmpeg-static ships an FFmpeg binary built with GPL components
(GPL-3.0-or-later). When redistributing Fusion Drama desktop installers
(dmg/exe) or Docker images that bundle this binary, you must comply with
the GNU GPL v3 for that component, including offering the corresponding
source. See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/gpl-3.0.html and
https://github.com/eugeneware/ffmpeg-static#license.

The ffprobe binary bundled via ffprobe-static is likewise GPL-3.0-or-later
and carries the same redistribution obligations as ffmpeg-static.

sharp's prebuilt binaries bundle libvips (LGPL-2.1-or-later). Distributing
binaries that link libvips requires allowing users to relink or replace the
LGPL component; shipping the unmodified official sharp prebuilds satisfies
this in practice. See https://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.

